  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="The Best Move May Be Forbidden" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;Cartesian x,y coordinates. Cyan: feasible ellipse. Straight lines: equal objective values. Gradient arrows show unit directions.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.0,0.0,0.06000000000000001],\&quot;size\&quot;:[7.15,7.15,0.8]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;aa771f44f8fce54078a29555a8fe4d04d3562ffc4be7d2ce8d7a1a1b233aa619\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;The objective is linear, f=cₓx+cᵧy, with ||c||=1. It has no unconstrained maximum on the whole plane. Restricting to a compact ellipse creates finite extrema.\&quot;,\&quot;The probe's allowed tangent is (−a sin θ,b cos θ). Its objective derivative is ∇f·p′(θ); vanishing means no first-order improvement along the curve, not a zero ambient gradient.\&quot;,\&quot;Arrow lengths are fixed to show unit gradient directions. Their alignment is meaningful; their displayed lengths do not represent the different gradient magnitudes.\&quot;,\&quot;For this ellipse g=x²/a²+y²/b², ∇g never vanishes on g=1. The maximum equals √((acₓ)²+(bcᵧ)²), and λ=maximum/2. The opposite point is the minimum, with negative λ.\&quot;,\&quot;The analytic extrema follow from Cauchy–Schwarz after mapping the ellipse to a unit circle. Lagrange multiplier equations alone do not classify stationary points in arbitrary constrained problems.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;lagrange\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;value\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Objective at probe c·p\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.529684374568977},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;maximum\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Analytic constrained maximum\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.6598044205117546},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;gap\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Maximum − current value\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.1301200459427776},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;tangent_derivative\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Feasible derivative df/dθ\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Zero at both extrema. θ parametrizes the ellipse, so this is not the derivative per unit arc length.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.644217687237691},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;gradient\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Unconstrained ||∇f||\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;The objective gradient is a nonzero constant even at constrained extrema.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.0},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;residual\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Maximum multiplier residual\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;||∇f−λ∇g|| with λ=maximum/2.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.0}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;axis_a\&quot;:2,\&quot;axis_b\&quot;:1,\&quot;direction\&quot;:0.7,\&quot;probe\&quot;:0},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;e1834618f60f4dabae2f429d11114901f9829ce89a433d9794a62b074fa013f4\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;The Best Move May Be Forbidden\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;planar\&quot;}&quot;" />
    </WorldInfo>
